></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Rheology of reconstituted type i collagen gel in confined compression.</article-title><source>Journal of Rheology</source><volume>41</volume><fpage>971</fpage><lpage>993</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005902-Tower1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tower</surname><given-names>TT</given-names></name><name><surname>Neidert</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Tranquillo</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Fiber alignment imaging during mechanical testing of soft tissues.</article-title><source>Ann Biomed Eng</source><volume>30</volume><fpage>1221</fpage><lpage>1233</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12540198</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005902-Girton1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Girton</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name><name><surname>Barocas</surname><given-names>VH</given-names></name><name><surname>Tranquillo</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Confined compression of a tissue-equivalent: collagen fibril and cell alignment in response to anisotropic strain.</article-title><source>J Biomech Eng</source><volume>124</volume><fpage>568</fpage><lpage>575</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12405600</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005902-Roeder1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roeder</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kokini</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Voytik-Harbin</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Local, three-dimensional strain measurements wi